From 066e9c04ecc930cecace231f303f6183317e898d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 06:01:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 03/33] drm/bridge: synopsys: dw-dp: Wait for the HPD state
 after runtime resume

Runtime resume reinitializes the controller, which restarts its HPD
state machine. The sink is reported as plugged only after it has held
HPD high for at least 100 ms, and resume sleeps a fixed 110 ms for that.

The margin is too small: with a DP Alt Mode dock that sends IRQ_HPD
Attentions while the controller is runtime suspended, the short pulse
handler resumes the controller and its first DPCD read can start before
the state machine reports the sink (and before the hot plug event that
the restart produces). That read then cannot succeed.

Poll the HPD state for up to 200 ms instead, as dw_dp_reset() does after
a controller reset. This waits only as long as needed when a sink is
present, and not at all when the Type-C side reports HPD low.

(cherry picked from commit 0e525158e7de122acaefc626e9704bd4c84e2b1e)

Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c | 15 ++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
index 8d66375804c1..b78a71beeb27 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/bridge/synopsys/dw-dp.c
@@ -2915,6 +2915,7 @@ EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(dw_dp_runtime_suspend);
 
 int dw_dp_runtime_resume(struct dw_dp *dp)
 {
+	u32 value;
 	int ret;
 
 	ret = clk_prepare_enable(dp->apb_clk);
@@ -2937,10 +2938,18 @@ int dw_dp_runtime_resume(struct dw_dp *dp)
 	enable_irq(dp->irq);
 
 	/*
-	 * HPD_HOT_PLUG bit is asserted only after the sink holds HPD
-	 * high for at least 100ms.
+	 * The HPD state machine restarts with the controller, and reports
+	 * the sink as plugged only after it has held HPD high for at least
+	 * 100 ms. Wait for that, so that the AUX transfers, detection or
+	 * short pulse handling that resumed the controller see the sink.
+	 * Nothing to wait for if the Type-C side reports HPD low.
 	 */
-	msleep(110);
+	if (dp->usbc_mode && !dp->usbc_hpd)
+		return 0;
+
+	regmap_read_poll_timeout(dp->regmap, DW_DP_HPD_STATUS, value,
+				 FIELD_GET(HPD_STATE, value) == DW_DP_HPD_STATE_PLUG,
+				 5000, 200000);
 
 	return 0;
 }
